<p>
    The following figure shows the failure surfaces of <span style="color: blue;">Tresca</span> and <span style="color: red;">von Mises</span> criteria in term of the principal stresses in 3 dimensions. 
    The 2D figure above can be found cenered around the origin in this plot. 
    The shape of the 2D failure surface <InlineEquation equation="(\\sigma_1,\\sigma_2)"/> remains the same, but moves location depending on <InlineEquation equation="\\sigma_3"/>.
    Just like in 2D, regions <strong>outside</strong> the surfaces are considered to have failed. 
</p>

